    "note": "Its long front faces Pine Street and the tower across it, behind a fenced yard (Greene's stereograph of the works), its north end on the 1871 plan's Pearson Street building line. Andreas (vol. 2, p. 69) puts the tower 'about one hundred feet to the west of the main building'; Greene's stereograph of the tower, taken from the burnt ground west of it, shows the works' long front behind the tower with its centre pavilion and the stack north of it. A camera solved on the tower's measured heights, the stack and three of the works' turrets puts the front about 50 m east of the tower's centre (Andreas's hundred feet is the open ground between them, read loosely) and its north end at Pearson Street's centre line, about 7 m further north than the 1871 plan's building line, which is within that plan's fit; the north end is held just behind the building line. The front's north end is local E 1190.0 N 1186.5.",
